{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not hate your brother in your heart.</b> Since the way of haters is to cover their hatred in their heart, as it says (Proverbs 26:24), \"With his lips he disguises hatred,\" Scripture uses the present tense. And it says, \"You shall surely reprove your fellow\" — a separate commandment, to teach him the reproof of discipline. \"And do not bear sin upon him\" — that you should bear guilt when he sins and you did not reprove him. This is why the language of Onkelos (Onkelos on Leviticus 19:17) inclines, as he said, \"וְלָא תְקַבֵּל עַל דִּילֵהּ חוֹבָא\" (and you shall not bear upon him punishment), that you should not accept punishment for his sin. And afterward He commanded that you love him. Now, one who hates his fellow transgresses a negative commandment, and one who loves him fulfills a positive commandment. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that \"הוֹכֵחַ תּוֹכִיחַ\" (you shall surely reprove) is like \"וְהוֹכִחַ אַבְרָהָם אֶת אֲבִימֶלֶךְ\" (and Abraham reproved Abimelech) (Genesis 21:25), and Scripture says: do not hate your brother in your heart when he does something against your will, but reprove him — \"Why did you do this to me?\" — and do not bear sin upon him by covering your hatred in your heart and not telling him, for when you reprove him he will defend himself to you, or he will repent and confess his sin and it will be atoned for him. And afterward He warns that you shall not take vengeance from him and shall not bear a grudge in your heart for what he did to you, for it is possible that one does not hate him but nevertheless remembers the offense in his heart; therefore He warns him to erase the transgression and sin of his brother from his heart. And afterward He commands that he love him as himself."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:56:08.524057540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}